 :problem
 {:source "surfaced while landing ADR-2607052000's first concrete increment (extending
           kotoba.turn.credential with a room/player-scoped mint/verify variant) -- the
           bare names turn/rt/net/signal don't self-document which external spec (if any)
           each repo implements, unlike the already-established org-<body>-<spec> family"
  :investigated
  ["read each repo's own docs/ADR-kotoba-{turn,rt,net,signal}-*.md in full before deciding
    a name, specifically to avoid overclaiming spec conformance in the name itself -- same
    failure mode the org-taxonomy rule already guards against (com-apple-{touchid,faceid}
    correctly uses the vendor com- scheme, not org-, because Apple's LocalAuthentication is
    proprietary not a published open spec)"
   "kotoba-lang/turn's ADR: message layer of IETF RFC 8656 (TURN) -- credential mint/verify
    (coturn use-auth-secret), STUN RFC 8489 codec, MESSAGE-INTEGRITY, FINGERPRINT. Clean
    external-spec port."
   "kotoba-lang/signal's ADR: the Signal Protocol (X3DH -> Double Ratchet, sender-keys
    group ratchet), signal.org. Clean external-spec port, org name IS the spec name (same
    shape as org-openusd/org-materialx)."
   "kotoba-lang/rt's ADR is explicit: 'this is deliberately NOT a WebSocket server' --
    kotoba's own room-membership/route-message contract, not a port of any single numbered
    external spec"
   "kotoba-lang/net's ADR is explicit: 're-implementing the entire libp2p stack... is not
    realistic' -- only loosely models GossipSub/Bitswap semantics as simplified pure-data
    functions, not a conformant libp2p port"]
  :risk "a repo name overclaiming spec conformance it doesn't have is worse than a boring
         bare name, since the name becomes the (mis)documentation"}

 :decision
 {:renames
  [{:old "turn" :new "org-ietf-turn"
    :rationale "IETF RFC 8656 (TURN) message layer -- clean spec port, same org-ietf-oauth2
                precedent (RFC-numbered IETF spec)"}
   {:old "signal" :new "org-signal"
    :rationale "Signal Protocol (signal.org) -- clean spec port, org name is the qualifier
                (org-openusd/org-materialx shape, no further -<spec> suffix needed)"}
   {:old "rt" :new "org-w3-webrtc-signaling"
    :rationale "NOT a spec port per its own ADR -- kotoba's own room-routing contract,
                named after the broader WebRTC signaling concept (W3C) it relays, per
                owner direction"}
   {:old "net" :new "io-libp2p"
    :rationale "NOT a libp2p port per its own ADR -- explicitly simplified GossipSub/
                Bitswap-inspired semantics only. Named after libp2p.io (literal-TLD
                reverse-domain io-<name> form) per owner direction -- distinct from
                org-<body>-<spec> and the compat-catalog's unconditional com-<vendor>
                (ADR-2607041500). First repo using this io- prefix; not yet a general
                doctrine."}]
  :deliberate_distinction
  "two of the four (rt, net) are explicitly NOT external-spec ports per their own ADRs --
   their new names describe the domain/concept they relate to, not spec conformance they
   don't have. Should not be flattened in future renames: a repo's name must never claim
   more spec conformance than its own ADR documents."
  :execution
  {:steps ["gh repo rename x4 (GitHub preserves old-name redirects)"
           "local checkout dir moved + remote retargeted, x4"
           "dependent repos: none found (grep across orgs/**/deps.edn for
            kotoba-lang/{turn,rt,net,signal} or matching :local/root paths -- zero hits)"
           "manifest/repos.edn: 4 new :path-overrides entries + 4 :extra-projects lines
            updated to new paths"
           "manifest/west.yml: bb scripts/gen-west-manifest.bb --entry
            org-ietf-turn,org-w3-webrtc-signaling,io-libp2p,org-signal (server-side pin
            verify OK), old 4 entries manually removed (--entry doesn't delete). Net
            project count unchanged (1462->1462), pure rename."
           "landed via GitHub Contents API single-entry commits directly to main, no
            branch/PR, per :manifest-workflow"]
   :caught_before_landing
   ["local org-ietf-turn checkout was one commit stale (missing the room/player-scoped-
     credential increment merged to main earlier this session) -- fast-forwarded before
     regenerating that entry's pin"
    "a concurrent session pushed an unrelated claude-lmstudio manifest entry mid-operation
     -- rebuilt the surgical rename diff against the latest GitHub tip instead of the
     slightly-stale local working copy, so that entry wasn't silently dropped"]}}

 :consequences
 {:no_behavior_change "name-only rename; kotoba.turn.credential's newly-added
                       mint-credential-scoped/verify-credential-scoped (commit 2d90bddc)
                       ship under org-ietf-turn from this point forward"
  :kami_engine_sdk_unaffected "turn.ts does not yet delegate to a compiled bridge from
                               org-ietf-turn -- remains explicit follow-up per
                               ADR-2607052000, unaffected by this rename"
  :naming_caveat "rt and net now carry names that could be misread as claiming full
                 external-spec conformance (WebRTC, libp2p) they explicitly disclaim in
                 their own ADRs -- consumers should read the repo's own docs/ADR-*.md
                 before assuming spec completeness from the name alone"}

 :alternatives []}
